# Build output is ignored by the per-project files instead, so each stays the
# standard template for its ecosystem: Backend/.gitignore (dotnet new gitignore)
# covers bin/ and obj/, Frontend/.gitignore (Vite) covers node_modules and dist.

# AI assistant working files - not part of the project itself
.claude
CLAUDE.md

# Secrets. Templates are committed as deploy/.env.example and
# deploy/edge/.env.example; the real files never are.
# A bare `.env` pattern matches only files named exactly that, so the
# webhook's env file needs its own entry - otherwise it sits untracked and
# a `git add -A` sweeps the deploy secret into a commit.
.env
webhook.env

# Database backups written on the server by deploy/backup.sh
deploy/backups/

# Deploy record appended by deploy/redeploy.sh on the server.
deploy/deploy.log
